# Without this file, git had no opinion on line endings: files were
# stored however whoever committed them happened to save them, and
# Windows' own core.autocrlf silently converted to CRLF on checkout
# here without ever normalizing the repository itself. A checkout on
# Linux (as qa-checks.yml runs on) got the raw stored bytes instead,
# which for most files was LF -- conflicting with .editorconfig's
# end_of_line = crlf for *.cs and failing dotnet format on nearly
# every file in the repository, despite an identical Windows checkout
# passing cleanly.
#
# This pins every text file to CRLF, matching .editorconfig, so a
# checkout is identical byte-for-byte on every platform.
* text=auto eol=crlf
